Let's calculate:

1 out of 200 randomly generated wands are WoWs.

Wands compromise 4% of items in main dungeon, 5% on the Rogue level and 
8% in the Gehennom. They also comprise 6% of items in containers.

13,5% of randomly generated tools are containers (excluding iceboxes and 
BoTs).

Tools compromise 8% of items in main dungeon, 0% on the Rogue level and 
12 % in the Gehennom. No tools are generated in containers.

So in main dungeon 4/100 + 6*13,5/10000 or 4,81% of random items are 
wands and thus 0,024% of random items are WoWs. That's 2,4 WoWs in ten 
thousand items.

On the Rogue level it's easy 5/100*1/200 so 2,5 WoWs in ten thousand 
items or 1 in 4000.

In the Gehennom we have a little better propability. That's (8/100 + 
12*13,5/10000)*1/200 that's 4,8 WoWs in ten thousand items. Exactly 
twice as much as in the main dungeon.

Except for the WoW in the Castle no other non randomly generated WoW's 
exist in the game.

